Proposed release-builder patch (NOT APPLIED). Written 2026-09-27 for the publication-boundary round;
revised the same day (follow-up round: P-1, P-2 and the assert note; nits round: 11 more ACCEPTED
entries per progress.md:286's "accept the 11" ruling, ACCEPTED now 16 keys).

Target: /home/brunner56/kp-release-20260927/  (package.py plus five CMake files in its source/ export)
Apply only after owner review, into a FRESH copy of the release folder (package.py refuses an existing
package/ and ZIP):   cd <fresh copy> && patch -p1 --dry-run < release-builder-proposed.patch
Checked with `patch -p1 --dry-run` against a /tmp copy of the 0927 inputs (6 files, clean). Nothing under
kp-release-* was touched.

What it changes
 package.py
  - Refuses to run under python -O or PYTHONOPTIMIZE (`if not __debug__: raise SystemExit`). Every
    acceptance check in this script is an assert, and -O removes asserts (review P-2).
  - Loads the hardened scanner (worktree tools/scan_release_zip.py, override with KP_SCANNER) and runs
    scanner.scan() on the finished ZIP as a mandatory gate. The ZIP is written as *.zip.unscanned and is
    renamed to the release name only when every finding is in ACCEPTED (16 reviewed exceptions, each with a
    reason: 5 from triage F3/F5/F8/F9, plus 11 /tmp findings accepted per the boundary-followup ruling in
    progress.md:286). verification.json gains privacy_scan, the accepted list and scanner_sha256.
  - The gate, the program-binary check and the ZIP-unchanged check exit with `raise SystemExit(...)`, not
    assert, so they hold even if the -O guard above is removed (review P-2).
  - Tar headers: uid=gid=0, uname=gname='', mtime=SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH (default 1790467200 =
    2026-09-27T00:00Z), mode 0644/0755. Gzip header: no file name, fixed mtime (triage M1, R5).
  - Excludes third_party/luajit/src/host/minilua, data/codecaves.toml and data/events.draft.toml
    (ruling 3; triage F6, F10, M2), and stops on any other ELF/PE/Mach-O/wasm bytes in the tarball (R3).
  - The receipt no longer lists private exclusion names (.superpowers/... etc.): they are counted and
    hashed instead (triage F2, R6).
 CMake (every i686-w64-mingw32-g++ custom command; add_compile_options does not reach them)
  - Compile lines gain, exactly:
        -ffile-prefix-map=${CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR}=. -ffile-prefix-map=${CMAKE_BINARY_DIR}=build
        -fmacro-prefix-map=${CMAKE_SOURCE_DIR}=.
    at CMakeLists.txt:94, src/hooks/hooks.cmake:92, src/api/structs.cmake:117,
       src/runtime/runtime.cmake:111, src/proxy/proxy.cmake:31  (line numbers in the ca329e5 export)
  - Link lines gain -s:  src/runtime/runtime.cmake:129 (kphasor.dll), src/proxy/proxy.cmake:31 (binkw32.dll)
  - No -DNDEBUG (orchestrator ruling: keep asserts). The maps and -s alone remove the paths. A verification
    rebuild of the 0927 source with exactly these flags (release-rebuild-verify.md) took kphasor.dll from 18
    scratch-root path strings to 0, and binkw32.dll had 0 before and after. The 18 ImGui IM_ASSERT __FILE__
    strings stay, mapped to ./..., and msvcrt!_assert is still imported. Imports, exports and .text/.data/
    .bss sizes are identical. -s renames .eh_frame to .eh_fram (C++ exceptions still caught in a wine DLL
    test) and drops the 4-byte .sxdata.
  - Correction to the earlier note: the project has no runtime assert() of its own. `grep -rnE
    '(^|[^_a-z])assert\(' src | grep -v static_assert` finds nothing, and no source includes <cassert> or
    <assert.h>. src/hooks/trampoline.hpp:46 is a static_assert, which NDEBUG does not affect. The only runtime
    asserts in kphasor.dll are ImGui's IM_ASSERT (→ assert → _assert), and NDEBUG would have turned those off.
  - Not covered: src/api/entity.cmake:90 and src/api/support.cmake:110 also call KP_MINGW_CXX, but neither
    object is linked into kphasor.dll or binkw32.dll (runtime.cmake:131-132). They need the same flags only if
    their objects ever ship.

